  "text_md": "this is true for the classical Tate curve. To glue each T with the rational Tate curve TQ, we will use an arithmetic fracture square, so the Cartesian diagram of E∞-rings\n\nB p B\n\n.\n\nBQ p B\n\nQ\n\nAs the functor Ellor(−)≃: CAlg → S is corepresented by TMF when restricted to complex periodic E∞-rings by Th.5.4, we have equivalences of spaces\n\nEllor(B)≃ ≃ MapCAlg(TMF,B) ≃ MapCAlg(TMF,BQ) ×\n\nMapCAlg(TMF,\n\nMapCAlg(TMF,( p B)Q)\n\np\n\nB)\n\n≃ Ellor(BQ)≃ ×\n\nEllor(\n\nEllor(( p B)Q)≃\n\np\n\nB)≃.\n\nWe already have the desired oriented elliptic curves T over each B and TQ over BQ, so to obtain T over B, it suﬃces to produce an isomorphism between oriented elliptic curves over\n\n( p B)Q. To do this, consider the equivalences of spaces\n\nEllor (\n\np\n\nB)Q\n\n≃\n\n≃ MapCAlg TMF,(\n\np\n\nB)Q ≃ MapCAlg\n\nQ\n\nTMFQ,(\n\np\n\nB)Q\n\n⊆ MapCAlg\n\nQ\n\ntmfQ,(\n\np\n\nB)Q) ≃ Ω∞+8 (\n\np\n\nB)Q × Ω∞+12 (\n\np\n\nB)Q , (5.5)\n\nwhere we use that tmfQ is the free E∞-Q-algebra on two generators c4 and c6 in degrees 8 and 12, respectively, that TMFQ ≃ tmfQ[∆−1] for ∆ = (c34 − c26)/1728, and that the containment above is a monomorphism onto those path components where the image of ∆ is invertible. Both the base-change of T and TQ to ( p B)Q are chosen such that the associated map from tmfQ sends c4 and c6 to their q-expansion maps. From the equivalences above, this shows that these oriented elliptic curves are equivalent over ( p B)Q. The fact that ( p B)Q has homotopy groups concentrated in even degrees also shows that the choice of equivalence is unique up to homotopy; even up to 3-homotopy. This yields the oriented elliptic curve T over B.\n\nTo compute the formal group associated with T, notice that B is an E∞-KU-algebra, as it then follows that the formal group associated with T is Gm. Indeed, by [Lur18b, Pr.4.3.23], an orientation on T is an equivalence between its associated formal group and the Quillen formal group over B. As the Quillen formal group of a complex-periodic E∞-ring satisﬁes base-change, we obtain the desired result of the Quillen formal group Gm over KU. Alternatively, one can use the fact that the space of oriented formal groups over a complex-periodic\n\n21\n\n",
